Z||000000||Phil||04-02-2000||12:16 PM||||New England Dragway had a $5 dial in day yesterday so after 40 yrs of driving I finally took a run down a real drag strip. About the only thing I did right was remember to turn the air conditioning off. I got there at 8:30 am and finally got to the line at 2:30 (lots of people). Spun the tires off the line , hit the rev limiter in both 1st and 2nd and my clutch slipped in 3rd and 4th. At least I beat the other guy with a 327 Chevelle or Nova or something all I know that it was blue. AnyWho wound up with a 14.33@94.7. If I ever get around to putting in a heavier clutch and practice my shifting and take offs  I can see a realistic shot into the 13s. See I'm already learning the excuse part of drag racing! Still it was fun and satisifed my curiousity.<BR>Slater<p>[This message has been edited by Phil (edited 04-02-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||04-02-2000||06:55 PM||||Not bad time for an old car with a funny name.  Too bad you didn't beat a red car.  The HD clutch in my car does wonders.  I used to be able to drive at 1500 rpm in 5th gear (40 mph), but no more.  The car wants 2000 rpm or it chatters.  My old clutch slipped a lot.  Now if you learn how to shift.<p>[This message has been edited by Old Lar (edited 04-02-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||04-02-2000||09:48 PM||||Red blue green orange (except yellow)all the same. I supposedly have a HD clutch (McLeod with dual friction disk) it only slips under heavy acceleraton at higher speeds 80+. I can drive along in 5th at 1500 no problem now. Oh well some day.||||reg||1
